#
# A parcel's charged weight in grams, in Sutra (caravan_rules.h CR1): the
# larger of its mass and its volume weight, the volume in cubic mm over the
# divisor in cubic mm per gram, rounded up to the next whole gram (5000 is
# the usual 5000 cubic cm per kg). mass fits 9(9), each side 9(5) mm and the
# divisor 9(5), so a negative or a wider one is refused, a divisor of 0 is
# a division Sutra refuses, and a charged weight past 9(9) does not fit.
# charged.tb says the same in Trebago.
record charged-weight
  mass: 9(9)
  length: 9(5)
  width: 9(5)
  height: 9(5)
  divisor: 9(5)
  volume: 9(15)
  charged: 9(9)
procedure
  compute volume = length * width * height
  compute charged = (volume + divisor - 1) / divisor
  if charged < mass
    compute charged = mass
  end-if
  answer charged
